[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-02f9e3c6-d62c-4f53-a220-e9ba7696c082\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Track</p><strong>Fri 2 May 2025 16:45 - 17:00 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/icse-2025/icse-2025-venue-canada-hall-1-and-2\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Canada Hall 1 and 2</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/icse-2025/icse-2025-research-track#program\" class=\"navigate\">Blockchain</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/danielamyot\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Daniel Amyot</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"02f9e3c6-d62c-4f53-a220-e9ba7696c082\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Definition and Detection of Centralization Defects in Smart Contracts</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><span class=\"pull-right\"><span class=\"output-badge\"><span class=\"label-primary label\">Blockchain</span></span></span><p>In recent years, security incidents stemming from centralization defects in smart contracts have led to substantial financial losses. A centralization defect refers to any error, flaw, or fault in a smart contract\u2019s design or development stage that introduces a single point of failure. Such defects allow a specific account or user to disrupt the normal operations of smart contracts, potentially causing malfunctions or even complete project shutdowns. Despite the significance of this issue, most current smart contract analyses overlook centralization defects, focusing primarily on other types of defects. To address this gap, our paper introduces six types of centralization defects in smart contracts by manually analyzing 597 Stack Exchange posts and 117 audit reports. For each defect, we provide a detailed description and code examples to illustrate its characteristics and potential impacts. Additionally, we introduce a tool named CDRipper (Centralization Defects Ripper) designed to identify the defined centralization defects. Specifically, CDRipper constructs a permission dependency graph (PDG) and extracts the permission dependencies of functions from the source code of smart contracts. It then detects the sensitive operations in functions and identifies centralization defects based on predefined patterns. We conduct a large-scale experiment using CDRipper on 244,424 real-world smart contracts and evaluate the results based on a manually labeled dataset. Our findings reveal that 82,446 contracts contain at least one of the six centralization defects, with our tool achieving an overall precision of 93.7%.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/zeweilin\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Zewei Lin<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Sun Yat-sen University</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/jiachichen2\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Jiachi Chen\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/jiachichen2/ee79be27-ddbd-46f1-81d6-d85b2c973791/micro-avatar?1783980698000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Jiachi Chen<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Sun Yat-sen University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/jiajingwu\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Jiajing Wu\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/jiajingwu/b92ee9ab-edcb-4ffc-b4fa-f5e0504ec352/micro-avatar?1783979503000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Jiajing Wu<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Sun Yat-sen University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/weizhezhang\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Weizhe Zhang<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Harbin Institute of Technology</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/icse-2025/zibinzheng1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Zibin Zheng\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/zibinzheng1/540bcac9-76b2-412d-b670-ad585a6bd7da/micro-avatar?1783970754000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Zibin Zheng<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">Sun Yat-sen University</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>China</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/icse-2025/icse-2025-research-track/129/Definition-and-Detection-of-Centralization-Defects-in-Smart-Contracts\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-02f9e3c6-d62c-4f53-a220-e9ba7696c082').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}, 'show');" },
